' Finance and banking: class model
' Companion notes: notes/finance.md — full stereotype legend: notes/stereotypes.md
'
' Role of credit in wage-labour and capital (Marx, Capital III; SPGB).
' Commercial banks are intermediaries: they lend existing funds (deposits,
' money-market borrowing, own capital). They do not create purchasing power
' out of thin air. Only the reserve / central bank issues new fiat currency.

@startuml finance
title V. Credit and banking — interest as a share of surplus value
caption Commercial banks intermediate; only the central bank issues fiat: notes/finance.md

hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<abstract det.>> #E3F2FD
  BackgroundColor<<social relation>> #EDE7F6
  BackgroundColor<<historically specific>> #FFEBEE
  BackgroundColor<<personification>> #FFF8E1
}

package "I. Surplus value is produced in production" as P1 {
  class SurplusValue <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    unpaid labour
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class Capital <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    value that valorizes itself
    (full definition: surplus-value-capital.puml)
  }
  class Capitalist <<personification>> {
    personification of industrial capital
  }
}

package "II. Sharing of surplus value" as P2 {
  class IndustrialProfit <<historically specific>> {
    part of s remaining with
    the functioning capitalist
  }
  class Interest <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    part of s paid for the use
    of money-capital
    not a second source of value
  }
  class InterestBearingCapital <<historically specific>> <<social relation>> {
    money lent as capital
    circuit : M – M'
  }
}

package "III. Commercial bank (intermediary)" as P3 {
  class CommercialBank <<historically specific>> {
    centralises lenders and borrowers
    lends only funds it has obtained
    profit = interest received − interest paid
  }
  class Banker <<personification>> {
    personification of
    interest-bearing capital
  }
  class IdleMoneyCapital <<historically specific>> {
    purchasing power generated
    in production, not yet spent
  }
  class Deposit <<historically specific>> {
    retail funds placed with the bank
    a loan from depositor to bank
  }
  class MoneyMarket <<historically specific>> {
    wholesale borrowing
    between banks and institutions
  }
  class Loan <<historically specific>> {
    advance of already-existing funds
    book entry is double-entry, not new wealth
  }
}

package "IV. Central / reserve bank (fiat issue)" as P4 {
  class CentralBank <<historically specific>> {
    issues legal-tender currency
    holds commercial banks' settlement accounts
  }
  class FiatCurrency <<historically specific>> {
    inconvertible state money
    notes, coin, reserve balances
  }
  class BankReserves <<historically specific>> {
    balances at the central bank
    used to settle inter-bank payments
    only the central bank can create these
  }
}

class ThinAirTheory <<abstract det.>> {
  {abstract}
  rejected claim: a commercial bank
  conjures new purchasing power
  by writing a deposit against a loan
}

Capital *-- SurplusValue : appropriates
SurplusValue --> IndustrialProfit : part retained as
SurplusValue --> Interest : part paid as
InterestBearingCapital --> Interest : claims
Capitalist --> IndustrialProfit : receives
Capitalist --> Interest : pays out of s
Capitalist --> Loan : borrows

IdleMoneyCapital --> Deposit : placed as
CommercialBank --> Deposit : borrows (retail)
CommercialBank --> MoneyMarket : borrows (wholesale)
CommercialBank --> Loan : advances obtained funds as
Banker --> CommercialBank : personifies
IdleMoneyCapital --> Loan : activated as\n(not created)
CommercialBank --> Interest : collects the spread

CentralBank --> FiatCurrency : issues
CentralBank --> BankReserves : creates
CommercialBank --> BankReserves : holds / settles with
Loan --> BankReserves : when spent, settled by\ntransfer of
ThinAirTheory ..> Loan : mistakes the book entry for
CommercialBank ..> ThinAirTheory : cannot enact
BankReserves ..> ThinAirTheory : settlement rules out

P1 -[hidden]right-> P2
P2 -[hidden]right-> P3
P3 -[hidden]down-> P4
ThinAirTheory -[hidden]up-> P4

note as NRole
  **Banks do not produce value (Capital III)**
  A bank centralises money-capital of
  lenders and of borrowers. Its profit
  is the difference between the rate
  at which it borrows and the rate
  at which it lends — a share of
  surplus value already produced.
end note

note bottom of ThinAirTheory
  BoE 2014 / Bundesbank passages that
  "lending creates deposits" describe
  double-entry bookkeeping. The same
  articles state that the loan must
  then be **funded** (reserves move
  when the borrower spends). That
  funding is existing money, not thin air.
end note

note right of CentralBank
  Fiat is managed state money.
  Only this institution issues new
  currency. A commercial bank that
  credits an account still has to
  obtain the funds that leave it.
end note

@enduml
